 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Notebook 04: Grounded Generation with Citations\n",
    "\n",
    "## Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "After retrieval, the system generates a grounded answer:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Question + Retrieved Evidence  -->  Build Context  -->  LLM Generation\n",
    "                                                              |\n",
    "                                                    Citation Validation\n",
    "                                                              |\n",
    "                                                    Claim Support Check\n",
    "                                                              |\n",
    "                                                     Grounded Answer\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**What you will see:**\n",
    "- How context is built from retrieved chunks\n",
    "- The system prompt that enforces citation-bound answers\n",
    "- How the LLM is called via Groq\n",
    "- How citations are validated\n",
    "- How claim support is checked independently\n",
    "\n",
    "**Prerequisites:** You need a `GROQ_API_KEY` in your `.env` file.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Source files:**\n",
    "- `src/rag_app/generation/prompt_builder.py` - System prompt and context construction\n",
    "- `src/rag_app/generation/citation.py` - Bilingual citation formatting\n",
    "- `src/rag_app/generation/generator.py` - Full generation pipeline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "project_root = Path.cwd()\n",
    "if str(project_root) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
    "\n",
    "from dotenv import load_dotenv\n",
    "load_dotenv()\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.rag_app import config\n",
    "from src.rag_app.retrieval.search import search\n",
    "from src.rag_app.generation.citation import citation_for, ARABIC_SECTIONS\n",
    "from src.rag_app.generation.prompt_builder import SYSTEM_PROMPT, output_instructions, build_context\n",
    "from src.rag_app.generation.generator import (\n",
    "    is_arabic,\n",
    "    refusal_output,\n",
    "    is_valid_answer,\n",
    "    claims_are_supported,\n",
    "    answer_recommendation,\n",
    "    claim_words,\n",
    "    get_generation_model,\n",
    "    generate,\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Retrieve Evidence"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "question = \"What follow-up is recommended after surgery?\"\n",
    "rows = search(question)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Question: '{question}'\")\n",
    "print(f\"Arabic: {is_arabic(question)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Retrieved {len(rows)} chunks (top score: {rows[0]['score']:.4f})\")\n",
    "for row in rows:\n",
    "    print(f\"  #{row['rank']} Page {row['page_number']}: {row['section_title']}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Build Context\n",
    "\n",
    "Each chunk is formatted as a `PASSAGE` with its citation. The LLM sees these passages and must answer only from them."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "arabic = is_arabic(question)\n",
    "context, allowed_citations = build_context(rows, arabic)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Context sent to the LLM:\")\n",
    "print(context[:800])\n",
    "print(\"...\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nAllowed citations ({len(allowed_citations)}):\")\n",
    "for c in allowed_citations:\n",
    "    print(f\"  {c}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. The System Prompt\n",
    "\n",
    "Key rules enforced:\n",
    "- Answer ONLY from retrieved passages\n",
    "- Refuse if passages don't directly answer\n",
    "- Use calibrated language (\"recommends\" vs \"suggests\")\n",
    "- Maximum 70-word recommendation + 80-word excerpt\n",
    "- Must include citation from the provided passages"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"SYSTEM PROMPT (first 500 chars):\")\n",
    "print(SYSTEM_PROMPT[:500])\n",
    "print(\"...\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nOUTPUT FORMAT (English):\")\n",
    "print(output_instructions(False))\n",
    "print(f\"\\nOUTPUT FORMAT (Arabic):\")\n",
    "print(output_instructions(True))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Generate Answer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if not os.getenv(\"GROQ_API_KEY\"):\n",
    "    print(\"WARNING: GROQ_API_KEY not set. Skipping LLM call.\")\n",
    "    print(\"Set it in .env to run this cell.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    answer = generate(question)\n",
    "    print(\"Generated answer:\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "    print(answer)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Citation Validation\n",
    "\n",
    "After generation, we verify that every citation in the answer exists in our `allowed_citations` set. This prevents the LLM from inventing sources."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example: valid vs invalid citations\n",
    "valid_answer = \"\"\"Recommendation:
    "Follow up with CEA testing and CT scans.\n",
    "\n",
    "Excerpt:\n",
    "Offer follow-up for detection of local recurrence.\n",
    "\n",
    "Citation:\n",
    "[Colorectal cancer, Section: 1.6 Ongoing care and support, Page: 26]\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "invalid_answer = \"\"\"Recommendation:\n",
    "Follow up with CEA testing and CT scans.\n",
    "\n",
    "Excerpt:\n",
    "Offer follow-up for detection of local recurrence.\n",
    "\n",
    "Citation:\n",
    "[Colorectal cancer, Section: 1.6 Ongoing care and support, Page: 26]\n",
    "[Colorectal cancer, Section: Made Up Section, Page: 99]\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "allowed = {\"[Colorectal cancer, Section: 1.6 Ongoing care and support, Page: 26]\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Valid answer:   {is_valid_answer(valid_answer, allowed, False)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Invalid answer: {is_valid_answer(invalid_answer, allowed, False)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Claim Support Check\n",
    "\n",
    "An independent lexical check ensures the recommendation text is actually supported by the retrieved evidence. This catches hallucinations that slip past citation validation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example: extracting the recommendation for claim checking\n",
    "sample_answer = \"\"\"Recommendation:\n",
    "The guideline recommends CEA testing every 3 months for 2 years after curative surgery.\n",
    "\n",
    "Excerpt:\n",
    "Offer CEA testing at follow-up appointments.\n",
    "\n",
    "Citation:\n",
    "[Colorectal cancer, Section: 1.6 Ongoing care and support, Page: 26]\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "recommendation_text = answer_recommendation(sample_answer, False)\n",
    "print(f\"Extracted recommendation: '{recommendation_text}'\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show claim words\n",
    "words = claim_words(recommendation_text)\n",
    "print(f\"Claim words (>2 chars): {sorted(words)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Refusal Handling\n",
    "\n",
    "The system refuses when:\n",
    "- No chunks are retrieved\n",
    "- Top score is below `MIN_RETRIEVAL_SCORE` (0.75)\n",
    "- The answer format is invalid\n",
    "- Claims are not supported by evidence\n",
    "- The question asks for stage-specific symptoms (NG12 doesn't classify by stage)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Show refusal outputs\n",
    "print(\"English refusal:\")\n",
    "print(refusal_output(False))\n",
    "print(\"\\nArabic refusal:\")\n",
    "print(refusal_output(True))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Arabic Question Example"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if not os.getenv(\"GROQ_API_KEY\"):\n",
    "    print(\"Skipping: GROQ_API_KEY not set.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    arabic_question = \"ايه المعلومات اللي المفروض فريق الرعاية يشرحوها لالperson المصاب بالسرطان؟\"\n",
    "    answer = generate(arabic_question)\n",
    "    print(f\"Question: '{arabic_question}'\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Arabic: {is_arabic(arabic_question)}\")\n",
    "    print(\"\\nGenerated answer:\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "    print(answer)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "| Step | Purpose |\n",
    "|------|---------|\n",
    "| Context building | Format retrieved chunks as numbered PASSAGEs with citations |\n",
    "| System prompt | Enforce citation-bound, calibrated, concise answers |\n",
    "| LLM generation | Groq API call (qwen3.6-27b, temperature=0.2, reasoning disabled) |\n",
    "| Citation validation | Verify every citation exists in our metadata |\n",
    "| Claim support check | Lexical/semantic verification that the recommendation is supported |\n",
    "| Refusal | Safe fallback when evidence is insufficient |\n",
    "| Disclaimer | Clinical safety notice on every answer |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Safety layers:**\n",
    "1. Retrieval score threshold (0.75)\n",
    "2. Answer format validation\n",
    "3. Citation metadata validation\n",
    "4. Claim-evidence support check\n",
    "5. Clinical disclaimer"
   ]
  }
 ],
